{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789229520,"nonce":"x0KTcoegdtWQdBPaTnrHisRIgCA=","message":"Fixed in 73cc01b.\n\nDynGet and GetI8/GetI16 results go through int_for_slot: a Bool slot holds `value != 0` (as the interpreter, Cranelift and HashLink read it; a plain trunc would have kept bit 0 only), a narrower or wider int slot the width-converted value. The interpreter's DynGet/GetI8/GetI16 now narrow through narrow_to_reg as well, with a Bool arm.\n\nHaxe never emits the shape, so crates/ash_cli/tests/retyped_reads.rs takes TestNarrowDynGet's bytecode, retargets each `DynGet dst; SafeCast narrow, dst` and `GetI8/GetI16 dst; ToInt narrow, dst` pair so the read writes the narrow register and the conversion becomes a Nop, and runs the result interpreted, in compiled-only mode (Cranelift installed synchronously; a hybrid arm on a program this short exits before any promotion lands) and as an AOT binary, with ASH_CHECK_REG_STORES=1. Without the fix the AOT arm reported \"storing i32 into an i8 slot OVERRUN\" for three findexes and printed different sums.","files":null}]}